From: GracedEternalKingCabbageMan
 <151803062+GracedEternalKingCabbageMan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:43:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bark: add testnet4 to the client's networks

The library already runs on any rust-bitcoin network, and the server
accepts testnet4, but the CLI and barkd only offered mainnet, signet,
mutinynet and regtest.

A testnet4 wallet also could not pay a BOLT11 invoice: such an invoice
carries the currency "tb", which testnet3 and testnet4 share, and
lightning-invoice maps it to Network::Testnet. Comparing that with the
wallet's network refused every testnet4 invoice. Compare currencies
instead, with a mapping that knows testnet4 (lightning-invoice's own
From<Network> maps it to regtest).
---
